  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Utah Tech University (UT), founded in 1911 and located in St. George, Utah, is a public institution offering a wide range of undergraduate programs across various disciplines. It ranks as the most affordable university in Utah. UT spans 117 acres, offering you state-of-the-art facilities. Not just that, with its accreditations from the Northwest Commission on Colleges and Universities (NWCCU) and other program-specific bodies, UT ensures that you receive a high-quality education.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>At UT, you’ll have a vibrant international community. This starts with the Office of International Programs, which ensures you have a great experience, from arrival to graduation. With a student-faculty ratio of 22:1, you’ll receive personalised teaching at UT. What’s more is that you can explore over 100 active student-led clubs, ranging from arts and culture to STEM and many more.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>Utah Tech offers you diverse housing options to suit your needs and budget. From apartment-style living at Abby Apartments and Chancellor Apartments to suite-style comfort at Campus View Suites I, II, and III, and the traditional experience at University Inn, you'll find the perfect fit.</p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><i>Additionally, if you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to </i><a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\"><i>download our app</i></a><i> and check out the Stays feature!</i></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Library</strong><br>Utah Tech’s library provides a wide array of online and on-site resources. The library boasts a vast collection of books and e-books, easily accessible through the online catalogue and research databases.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong><br>You can enjoy many sports activities at UT through their Club Sports and Intramurals. You can compete against fellow students in several activities, including flag football, basketball, softball, sand volleyball, soccer, and more. You can also get personal training, pop-up classes, group fitness, and more, through Utah Tech’s Fitness &amp; Wellness.</p><p><strong>Cafeteria</strong><br>Utah Tech Dining Services provides a variety of on-campus dining options. You can choose a meal plan that suits your taste and budget. Popular dining locations include the Trailblazers Cafe, Brooks' Stop, Stacks, and Grazers, each with different menus and atmospheres.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
